  "algorithm": "Independently authored four-neighbor Dirichlet correction: solve discrete Laplace(delta)=0 inside the binary domain, with source-minus-generated boundary values on known neighbors. Add delta to generated RGB inside the domain and copy known source f32 bits everywhere else. Equivalent gradient-guided Poisson insertion without mixed gradients. No selected original pixels in RHS, no resampling/clipping, no inferred unknown texture, no tile blending claim.",
  "numeric_scope": "Solve f64, return f32. PyAMG classical Ruge-Stuben hierarchy preconditions CG for each channel, tol1e-8/max100; independently recomputed relative residual must be finite and <=1e-6 before return. Bounded1.8MP interior domain; touching context-edge rejects and requires more known context. No render-loop or slider integration.",
